{
 "_about": "What stands in each night-market room (docs/maps/night_market.md): doors, pickups, crates, townsfolk and examine spots. Same shape as world/placements.json; Main lays this file over it in slice mode (Placements.extra_ids), so market ids (mk_*) sit beside the old Harrow ids and the classic game never sees them. 'room' is the room id in slice/rooms.json; the room scene holds the node and its placement_id, this file the contents and the rules. All spoken words are the Writer's PLACEHOLDERS (VS-31) in data/dialogue/market_placeholder.json, slice_scenes.json and junkyard_placeholder.json; final text at VS-37 (Dialogue & writing is Level 0). VS-31 also added ambient barks (bark_radius_m, barks) to the chatty townsfolk and story-state variants: _taken (job_main_taken, not kasp_beaten) and _party (market_party, set by the ending scenes in slice/story_scenes.json); Mox's first talk runs the mox_deck scene and the first Gate 4 grunt talk after taking the job runs gate_pass. No fighting in town; the patrol wolves are scenery. Gate 4's barrier door needs the flag job_main_taken (set by taking the main job at the Dispatch Counter; the Courier Pass is handed over with it, see slice/jobs.json). Its target junk_j1 is not built yet (see slice/rooms.json pending_rooms).",
